{"ingredient/pandan":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/pandan","n":"Pandan","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 13 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Pandanus amaryllifolius is a tropical plant in the Pandanus (screwpine) genus, which is commonly known as pandan ( or  ~  PUN-done; Malay: [ˈpandan]). Its fragrant leaves are commonly used for flavoring in the cuisines of Southeast Asia, some South Asian cuisines (such as Sri Lankan cuisine) and in the Hainanese cuisine from China."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-pandan"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandanus_amaryllifolius"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Klepon","dish/klepon"],["Kolak (food)","dish/kolak-food"],["Nasi bogana","dish/nasi-bogana"],["Pohulpohul","dish/pohulpohul"],["Timphan","dish/timphan"],["Wajik","dish/wajik"]]],["Acehnese cuisine","cuisine/acehnese-cuisine",[["Timphan","dish/timphan"]]],["Betawi cuisine","cuisine/betawi-cuisine",[["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"]]],["Malay cuisine","cuisine/malay-cuisine",[["Akok (food)","dish/akok-food"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Palm sugar","ingredient/palm-sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Brown sugar","ingredient/brown-sugar"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Rice flour","ingredient/rice-flour"],["Margarine","ingredient/margarine"],["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Glutinous rice","ingredient/glutinous-rice"],["Banana","ingredient/banana"],["Adzuki bean","ingredient/adzuki-bean"],["Black turtle bean","ingredient/black-turtle-b